1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,059
The exact audit freezes prompts, seeds, field size, renderer, frame indices, semantic evaluator, and pass thresholds before execution.

2
00:00:09,059 --> 00:00:14,873
It renders frames zero, twenty-four, and forty-eight at one-forty-four by two-sixteen.

3
00:00:14,873 --> 00:00:26,027
OpenCLIP ViT-B thirty-two embeds each frame, normalized frame embeddings are mean-pooled, and the resulting video vector is compared against the three exact prompts.

4
00:00:26,027 --> 00:00:31,368
The preregistration prevents a visually appealing seed from redefining success.

5
00:00:32,068 --> 00:00:38,589
Top-one retrieval asks whether a correct generated field is closest to its intended prompt among three choices.

6
00:00:38,589 --> 00:00:48,166
The shuffled generation margin instead holds the intended text fixed and compares a correctly conditioned field against a field actually generated from wrong text.

7
00:00:48,166 --> 00:00:51,103
Null margin does the same with no semantic prompt.

8
00:00:51,103 --> 00:00:55,392
Pairwise win counts retain seed-level information that a mean could hide.

9
00:00:55,392 --> 00:01:01,091
All are needed because any one semantic score can be fooled by class imbalance or evaluator bias.

10
00:01:01,791 --> 00:01:06,788
Across nine exact prompt programs, intended retrieval succeeds eight times.

11
00:01:06,788 --> 00:01:09,587
Every prompt class has majority retrieval.

12
00:01:09,587 --> 00:01:19,381
Mean correct-minus-shuffled generation similarity is plus zero-point-zero-five-six-four-eight, above the frozen plus zero-point-zero-two threshold.

13
00:01:19,381 --> 00:01:25,911
Correct-minus-null is plus zero-point-zero-three-three-four-eight, above plus zero-point-zero-one.

14
00:01:25,911 --> 00:01:29,576
Correct wins all nine shuffled and all nine null pairs.

15
00:01:29,576 --> 00:01:35,173
Counts, donor distinction, finite rendering, and continuous-center checks also pass.

16
00:01:35,873 --> 00:01:44,183
Gate two-b-one replaces exact lookup with a five-hundred-forty-one-thousand-two-hundred-twenty-three-parameter autoregressive network.

17
00:01:44,183 --> 00:01:47,408
Frozen text embeddings enter a two-layer projection.

18
00:01:47,408 --> 00:01:50,570
A scene head predicts one of three semantic tokens.

19
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:53,485
Scene embedding conditions the foreground head.

20
00:01:53,485 --> 00:01:57,578
Text, scene, and sampled foreground condition the background head.

21
00:01:57,578 --> 00:02:03,531
Source logits are not masked by scene; only exact foreground-background repetition is forbidden.

22
00:02:03,531 --> 00:02:07,872
Scene-consistent donors must therefore be learned rather than imposed.

23
00:02:08,572 --> 00:02:17,950
Training uses two authored paraphrases plus the exact prompt for each class and enumerates ordered donor pairs, while reserving cyclic pairs for evaluation.

24
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:22,518
The held-out set changes both wording and foreground-background combination.

25
00:02:22,518 --> 00:02:25,884
Ten percent empty-text dropout teaches a null condition.

26
00:02:25,884 --> 00:02:37,967
Correct, cyclic-shuffled, and empty embeddings score the identical target programs, which makes token negative log likelihood a clean conditional test before any renderer or CLIP model enters the loop.

27
00:02:38,667 --> 00:02:43,385
The best correct-condition negative log likelihood occurs at step one hundred.

28
00:02:43,385 --> 00:02:46,227
Evaluation continues every one hundred updates.

29
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:52,941
Ten consecutive evaluations through step eleven hundred fail to improve it, satisfying the frozen plateau rule.

30
00:02:52,941 --> 00:03:03,224
Correct held-out NLL is two-point-two-zero-zero-five, compared with four-point-three-eight-seven under cyclic-shuffled wording and two-point-five-three-nine-one for null.

31
00:03:03,224 --> 00:03:07,397
Scene accuracy is one hundred percent for correct unseen paraphrases.

32
00:03:07,397 --> 00:03:12,357
This is evidence of early overfit, not evidence that the run was simply too short.

33
00:03:13,057 --> 00:03:19,225
All nine correct-text samples predict the right scene and emit both unmasked donors from that scene.

34
00:03:19,225 --> 00:03:26,196
Rendered correct-minus-shuffled and correct-minus-null margins pass, and correct beats shuffled in seven of nine.

35
00:03:26,196 --> 00:03:33,783
But raw three-way OpenCLIP top-one is only four of nine, below the required six, with majority retrieval in only one class.

36
00:03:33,783 --> 00:03:35,202
We retain that failure.

37
00:03:35,202 --> 00:03:44,825
The learned network understands the tiny program syntax and causal scene conditioning; it does not yet establish robust open-vocabulary semantic generation.
